  "question": {
    "text": "The absolute difference between the squares of the radii of the two circles passing through the point $(-9,4)$ and touching the lines $x+y=3$ and $x-y=3$, is equal to ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "768",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/YdibDgiQwZs7CoX8ECy9A5iG0ET1hQZRhKjP1D0Ervs.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>Centre $(\\mathrm{a}, 0)$<br/>$\\mathrm{r}=\\left|\\frac{\\mathrm{a}-0-3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right|$<br/>$\\operatorname{circle}(x-a)^2+y^2=\\left(\\frac{a-3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2$<br/>passes through $(-9,4)$<br/>$2\\left(a^2+18 a+81+16\\right)=\\left(a^2-6 a+9\\right)$<br/>$\\mathrm{a}^2+42 \\mathrm{a}+185=0$<br/>$(a+37)(a+5)=0$<br/>$\\Rightarrow a=-37,-5$<br/>$r_1=\\left|\\frac{-37-3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right|=20 \\sqrt{2}$<br/>$\\mathrm{r}_2=\\left|\\frac{-5-3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right|=4 \\sqrt{2}$<br/>$\\left|r_1^2-r_2^2\\right|=|800-32|=768$",
    "image": null
  },
